  "step_3": "The decision reason prefers the lottery without a sure outcome. However, the individual explicitly chooses the lottery with the sure outcome (Lottery B) because of its certainty. The information considered by the individual (the presence of a sure outcome in B and the absence in A) matches the information relevant to the reason. But the individual’s justification—choosing the sure outcome—directly contradicts the rule of the reason, which would prefer the lottery without a sure outcome (i.e., Lottery A). Therefore, although the individual is aware of the presence of a sure outcome, they use it as a reason to prefer Lottery B, which is the opposite of what the decision reason prescribes. Thus, the individual did not use the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

